Okay, now, we are gonna work with one of the core functions of linked list, that is "Push_Front"
So, while doing push_front, we will encounter 2 cases, first one is when the list is totally empty
and the second one is when there is an element in the list.

1.First Case:

So, in the first case, when the list is empty, the head pointer (Node*head) is gonna be NULL.
And the tail pointer (Node*tail) is gonna be NULL too. So, in order to push an element to the
front, we will have to follow two steps
1. Create a node--> that will store the data
2. Point the head pointer(Node*head) and the tail pointer (Node*tail) to the new node

2. Second Case:

So, in the second case, the list is not empty, and the head pointer(Node*head) is pointing to
the first element of the list. SO, in order to add another element, we will have to follow the 
following steps:
1. Create a new node--> this will continue regardless whether there is an element or not
2. Dereference the newNode pointer and use its 'next' property to point it to the 'head' newNode->next=head
3. head=newNode; 
